        <h3 class="close">Previous Updates - Archives</h3>
        <!-- previous entries -->
	    <p><a href="articles/11_09_02.html">Inside Paillard Bolex</a><br>
	    <span class="italicb">September 2, 2011 -- Friday</span><br>
	      Four short films, that provide a fascinating look inside the Paillard Bolex factory in Saint-Croix.
		  </p>
		<p><a href="news/08-christmas.html">Happy Holidays</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">December 4, 2008 -- Thursday</span><br>
		  A short holiday-themed update, and explanation for the lack of recent updates.
		  </p>		
		<p>
		  <span class="italicb">September 24, 2008 -- Wednesday</span><br>
		  The discussion forum is currently down for upgrades.
		  </p>		
		<p>
		  <span class="italicb">June 6, 2008 -- Friday</span><br>
		  New site design: centered for higher resolution monitors. Refresh your browser if things look odd.
		  </p>		
		<p><a href="articles/07_05_11.html">Bolex Serial Numbers</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">May 11, 2007 -- Friday</span><br>
		  New Article: a list of camera serial numbers and dates of manufacture. The camera section has also been updated with more information.
		  </p>		
		<p><a href="articles/07_04_23.html">TV Commercial for Bolex 155 Macrozoom</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">April 23, 2007 -- Monday</span><br>
		  A Bikini, a Beach and a Bolex?  This video for a 1968 television commercial features all three.
		  </p>		
		<p><a href="articles/07_04_22.html">1958 TV Commercial for Bolex Cameras</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">April 22, 2007 -- Sunday</span><br>
		  New article with video: A classic television commercial from 1958, promoting Paillard-Bolex and Willoughby's camera store.
		  </p>		
		<p><a href="projectors.html">Bolex Projector Serial Numbers</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">April 11, 2007 -- Wednesday</span><br>
		  I've added serial numbers and dates of manufacture for all Paillard models on the projector page, starting with the <a href="projectors/model-g.html">Model G</a>.
		  </p>		
		<p><a href="ephemera/books50.html">Bolex Books from the 1950s and 60s</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">March 29, 2007 -- Thursday</span><br>
		  Added four book cover scans to the ephemera section, thanks to contributions from a German collector. They're also ordered chronologically now.
		  </p>		
		<p><a href="articles/07_03_21.html">Lenses for Bolex 16mm Cameras</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">March 21, 2007 -- Wednesday</span><br>
		  Explained: The differences between regular and RX lenses for Bolex H16 cameras.
		  </p>		
		<p><a href="auctions.html">Current eBay Auctions</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">March 10, 2007 -- Saturday</span><br>
		  Added a new page that continuously lists 50 Bolex related auctions ending soon on eBay.
		  </p>		
		<p><a href="http://www.bolexcollector.com/forums/">New Bolex Discussion Forum!</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">March 2, 2007 -- Friday</span><br>
		  Read messages or join the community to talk with others about Bolex (or any classic movie cameras and projectors.)
		  </p>		
		<p><a href="ephemera/catalog50.html">1950s Bolex Catalogs</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">February 27, 2007 -- Tuesday</span><br>
		  New additions to the section on Bolex product catalogs for movie equipment from the 1950s.
		  </p>		
		<p><a href="news/07-february.html">News: February '07 Updates</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">February 22, 2007 -- Thursday</span><br>
		  Site news, updates and additions, including a list of 10 new scans of Bolex brochures to the ephemera section.
		  </p>		
		<p><a href="articles/07_02_06.html">Bolex Dealer Camera Display Stand</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">February 6, 2007 -- Tuesday</span><br>
		  New Article: Images and details of a decorative camera display stand used in franchised Bolex dealer stores during the 1950s.
		  </p>		
		<p>
		  <span class="italicb">January 28, 2007 -- Sunday</span><br>
		  In response to a few email questions I've received regarding shutter speeds, I have updated the F.A.Q. with this: <a href="faq.html#310">"How to determine your exposure time"</a>.
		  </p>
		<p><a href="articles/07_01_26.html">We Visit Paillard-Bolex</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">January 26, 2006 -- Friday</span><br>
		  New Article: An <i>Amateur Movie Maker</i> team takes a trip to a Swiss mountain top to investigate the facts behind the magic name. (circa 1959)
		  </p>		
		<p>
		  <span class="italicb">January 23, 2007 -- Tuesday</span><br>
		  Several updates, thanks to reader contributions: H. Kriesi has supplied more information on the <a href="projectors/auto-proj.html">Auto Cine projector</a>; A <a href="ephemera/ads50_ad031.html">UK C8S ad</a>, courtesy J. Exley; and <a href="articles/06_11_08.html">this mystery camera</a> has been identified.
		  </p>
		<p>
		  <span class="italicb">January 13, 2007 -- Saturday</span><br>
		  J. Martin of Switzerland has provided us with two excellent Bolex ads from 1931. Both have been added to the ephemera section, <a href="ephemera/ads40_ad019.html">here</a> and <a href="ephemera/ads40_ad020.html">here</a>.
		  </p>
		<p>
		  <span class="italicb">January 8, 2007 -- Monday</span><br>
		  The first of many additions for 2007 -- A magazine advertisement from 1947. You can <a href="ephemera/ads40_ad018.html">view it here</a>. More on the way soon.
		  </p>
		<p><a href="news/06-christmas.html">Merry Christmas, from Bolex Collector</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">December 18, 2006 -- Monday</span><br>
		  Seasons Greetings and site related news for 2007.
		  </p>		
		<p><span class="italicb">December 6, 2006 -- Wednesday</span><br>
		  Made some minor typo and link corrections to the site. Also, the identity of <a href="articles/06_11_08.html">this camera</a> was found. The answer will be posted soon, but you're still welcome to send in your guesses.
		  </p>
		<p><a href="articles/06_12_02.html">Bolex Christmas Gift Ideas</a><br>
		  <span class="italicb">December 2, 2006 -- Saturday</span><br>
		  An interactive guide to Bolex cameras and accessories, including prices - as of Christmas 1959, that is.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_11_12.html">Shoot Your Own Thanksgiving Turkey</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">November 12, 2006 -- Sunday</span><br>
          You don't have to celebrate Thanksgiving to enjoy this classic article 
          from the Fall 1960 issue of the Bolex Reporter magazine.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_11_10.html">Bolex Glass Dealer Sign</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">November 10, 2006 -- Friday</span><br>
          Images and details of a piece from my collection.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_11_09.html">Three-Lens Turret Conversion</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">November 9, 2006 -- Thursday</span><br>
          A scan of some interesting ephemera from May 1959.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_11_08.html">"What Is It?"</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">November 8, 2006 -- Wednesday</span><br>
          New article: just something interesting I found in a 1968 camera magazine. 
          </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_10_27.html">Bolex Music</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">October 27, 2006 -- Friday</span><br>
          New Article: A 45 rpm record with music and sound effects for adding 
          to your films.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_10_26.html">Bolex Record - Ross Hunter</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">October 26, 2006 -- Thursday</span><br>
          A Bolex instructional record from 1961, titled "Top Secrets of Hollywood 
          Movie Making", with tips from producer Ross Hunter.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_10_12.html">Bolex Logo Dealer Sign</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">October 12, 2006 -- Thursday</span><br>
          Details and pictures of an aluminum Dealer sign in the shape of the 
          Paillard-Bolex logo.
		  </p>
        <p><span class="italicb">October 8, 2006 -- Sunday</span><br>
          I updated the comments section on the <a href="cameras/b8.html">Bolex 
          B-8</a> camera page to include images and serial numbers of the different 
          types of control dials found on early B-8 and <a href="cameras/c8.html">C-8</a> 
          cameras. Hope you find this useful.
		  </p>
        <p><span class="italicb">October 5, 2006 -- Thursday</span><br>
          Another advertisement; this one, from a 1948 magazine. Somehow, I'd 
          never noticed it before today... so, I scanned it. <a href="ephemera/ads40_ad017.html">Have 
          a look</a>.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_10_04.html">The Bolex Reporter Magazine</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">October 4, 2006 -- Wednesday</span><br>
          A look at the Bolex Reporter magazine, published from 1950 to 1974 by 
          Paillard Incorporated in the United States.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_09_20.html">Small Bolex Items</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">September 20, 2006 -- Wednesday</span><br>
          A couple of, presumably, Bolex dealer items; a Paillard-Bolex tie-bar 
          and cufflink.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_08_17.html">Tips on Mercury Battery Replacement</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">August 17, 2006 -- Thursday</span><br>
          New article added, with suggestions for replacement batteries on cameras 
          that use obsolete mercury cells.
		  </p>
        <p> <span class="italicb">July 25, 2006 -- Tuesday</span><br>
          Ephemera additions: 10 more magazine ads from the 1940s and 10 more 
          brochures from the late '50s and early '60s. View them beginning on 
          <a href="ephemera/ads40.html">this</a> page.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_04_26.html">The American Bolex Company</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">April 26, 2006 -- Wednesday</span><br>
          A brief history of the sole distributor of Paillard products in the 
          United States from 1936 to 1948, and manufacturer of Ambol and Cinea 
          motion picture equipment.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/06_01_01.html">Leader, Standard or Deluxe?</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">January 1, 2006 -- Sunday</span><br>
          How to identify the differences between these three very similar models. 
          More importantly, why it doesn't really matter.
		  </p>
        <p><a href="articles/05_12_01.html">The Paillard-Bolex Camera</a><br>
          <span class="italicb">December 1, 2005 -- Thursday</span><br>
          A general look at the different models of Bolex cameras, from the professional 
          H model, to the pocket size 8mm home movie camera.
		  </p>
